---
// The control plane / nodes split, for lesson 3.
//
// Static SVG rather than the runtime-built markup the two interactives use, so
// Astro's scoped styles would work here. It still uses Tailwind utilities
// instead, because `darkMode: ["class"]` means `dark:` variants already handle
// both themes and the rest of the courses components are written that way.
//
// Arrowheads are drawn as paths rather than `<marker>` elements: a marker does
// not inherit the referencing element's colour in every browser, so a themed
// line would end in a black head in one of the two themes.
//
// The viewBox is kept narrow (560 wide) and the type generous so the whole
// thing stays legible when it scales down on a phone. The wrapper scrolls
// rather than letting the article itself scroll sideways.
---

<figure class="not-prose my-8 overflow-x-auto">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 560 300"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="cluster-split-title cluster-split-desc"
    class="mx-auto block h-auto w-full min-w-[340px] max-w-[560px]">
    <title id="cluster-split-title">A cluster, split into a control plane and nodes</title>
    <desc id="cluster-split-desc">
      One cluster contains two parts. The control plane decides what should happen. The nodes run
      the containers. The control plane tells the nodes what should be running, and the nodes
      report back what is actually running.
    </desc>

    <text x="22" y="26" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="15" font-weight="600">
      Cluster
    </text>
    <rect
      x="12"
      y="38"
      width="536"
      height="246"
      rx="14"
      fill="none"
      stroke-dasharray="6 5"
      class="stroke-gray-300 dark:stroke-gray-700"
      stroke-width="1.5"
    />

    <g class="fill-gray-50 stroke-gray-300 dark:fill-gray-900 dark:stroke-gray-700" stroke-width="1.5">
      <rect x="32" y="76" width="190" height="150" rx="10" />
      <rect x="338" y="76" width="190" height="150" rx="10" />
    </g>

    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="127" y="130" class="fill-gray-900 dark:fill-gray-100" font-size="19" font-weight="600">
        Control plane
      </text>
      <text x="127" y="160" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="14">decides what</text>
      <text x="127" y="180" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="14">should happen</text>

      <text x="433" y="130" class="fill-gray-900 dark:fill-gray-100" font-size="19" font-weight="600">
        Nodes
      </text>
      <text x="433" y="160" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="14">run the</text>
      <text x="433" y="180" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="14">containers</text>
    </g>

    <g class="stroke-gray-400 dark:stroke-gray-500" stroke-width="1.5">
      <line x1="230" y1="124" x2="320" y2="124" />
      <line x1="330" y1="178" x2="240" y2="178" />
    </g>
    <g class="fill-gray-400 dark:fill-gray-500">
      <path d="M320 119 L332 124 L320 129 Z" />
      <path d="M240 173 L228 178 L240 183 Z" />
    </g>

    <g text-anchor="middle" class="fill-gray-500 dark:fill-gray-400" font-size="13">
      <text x="280" y="110">should be running</text>
      <text x="280" y="202">actually running</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</figure>
